COMMENTS.COMMENT:
eeprom_verify_xor_checksum(int param_1)
FIRMWARE-VERIFIED (NML_bin.c:25848)

param_1 = g_EEPROM_Shadow_Buffer (0x8024e4d4)
Called as eeprom_verify_xor_checksum(-0x7fdb1b2c)
  -0x7fdb1b2c == 0x8024e4d4 in unsigned 32-bit MIPS.

Algorithm:
  ushort acc = 0;
  for (uint i = 0xC0; i < 0x400; i++)
      acc ^= *(ushort*)(param_1 + i*2);
  return acc == 0xFFFF;

Covers bytes 0x180-0x7FE of EEPROM image.
Word 0x3FF (byte 0x7FE) is the checksum word.
Called before sys_flash_write_block() - NOT during tag 0x86/0x87 reads.

XPP_PBKDF2_F_Block [PBKDF2-SHA1 F function -- NEVER CALLED, WPA GAP 2c dead code] *** WPA GAP 2 -- fully implemented, never called ***
Standard PBKDF2-SHA1 one block computation (RFC 2898 Section 5.2). Call twice to produce 32-byte WPA PMK from ASCII passphrase:
// Block 1: G_WPA_PMK[0..19] XPP_PBKDF2_F_Block( passphrase, // param_1: null-terminated key string ssid, // param_2: salt buffer ssid_len, // salt length 4096, // iterations (WPA standard) 1, // block index i &G_WPA_PMK[0] // output: 20 bytes );
// Block 2: G_WPA_PMK[20..31] (only first 12 bytes used) XPP_PBKDF2_F_Block( passphrase, ssid, ssid_len, 4096, 2, &G_WPA_PMK[20] );
MUST run in worker task context (wireless_worker_task or equivalent). Takes 100-200ms per block at MN-740 MIPS clock speed. Running inline in the TLV parse handler would stall all XPP processing for 200-400ms total.
Scheduling: set G_WPA_PBKDF2_Pending flag in Tag 0x12 handler, check flag in wireless_worker_task after XPP_Type02_0x07_FlashConfig returns, call PBKDF2 x2, copy result to G_WPA_PMK, set G_WPA_PMK_Ready flag, clear G_WPA_PBKDF2_Pending.

NET_Process_Interface_Chain [Walks the interface linked list, applies config/dispatch to each node]
while param_1 != 0: NET_Apply_Config_To_Interface(param_1, param_2, param_3, param_4) param_1 = *(param_1 + 4) (follow next ptr)
Called from WLAN_RX_Frame_Decapsulate_And_Scan_Process after 802.11 decap to push the resulting Ethernet frame up the network stack for XPP type dispatch. Terminates on NULL next ptr -- typically 2 nodes: ETH0 (XPP) + WLAN0 (data).

